@startuml
title UML State Chart Diagram

state "Registration/Login" as RL
RL : entry / User enters details
RL : do / Verify credentials
RL : exit / Access system

state "Teacher Mode" as TM
TM : entry / Login successful (Teacher)
TM : do / Perform teacher actions
TM : exit / Access teacher functionalities

state "Student Mode" as SM
SM : entry / Login successful (Student)
SM : do / Perform student actions
SM : exit / Access student functionalities

state "Create Quiz" as CQ
CQ : entry / Teacher in TM
CQ : do / Create new quiz
CQ : exit / Quiz created

state "Edit Quiz" as EQ
EQ : entry / Teacher in TM
EQ : do / Edit existing quiz
EQ : exit / Quiz edited

state "Save/Post Quiz" as SPQ
SPQ : entry / Teacher in TM
SPQ : do / Save as draft or post
SPQ : exit / Quiz saved/posted

state "View Results" as VR
VR : entry / Teacher in TM, Quiz completed
VR : do / View quiz results
VR : exit / Results displayed

state "Select Quiz" as SQ
SQ : entry / Student in SM, Quiz available
SQ : do / Select a quiz
SQ : exit / Quiz selected

state "Answer Quiz" as AQ
AQ : entry / Student in SM, Quiz selected
AQ : do / Answer quiz questions
AQ : exit / Quiz answered

state "Submit Quiz" as SU
SU : entry / Student in SM, Quiz answered
SU : do / Submit quiz
SU : exit / Quiz submitted

state "View Result" as VSR
VSR : entry / Student in SM, Quiz submitted
VSR : do / View quiz result
VSR : exit / Result displayed

RL --> TM : Successful login (Teacher)
RL --> SM : Successful login (Student)
TM --> CQ : Create new quiz
TM --> EQ : Edit existing quiz
TM --> SPQ : Save/Post quiz
TM --> VR : View results
SM --> SQ : Select quiz
SQ --> AQ : Answer quiz
AQ --> SU : Submit quiz
SU --> VSR : View result
CQ --> SPQ : Save/Post quiz
EQ --> SPQ : Save/Post quiz
SPQ --> [*]
VR --> [*]
VSR --> [*]

@enduml
